// A choreography for the robot dancer "dancer.py" of folder "osc_resources" (line "-py.dancer" above), with the output format "Real-time OSC".
// Click START THE ROBOT to open its window.
// See https://bolprocessor.org/robot-puppet/ and https://bolprocessor.org/usage-in-robotics/


// Here the gestures are time-objects (sound-objects) of "-so.robot_objects", named in "-al.robot_objects": armsup, armsdown, clap, wave, waveoff, nod.
// Each prototype contains a Csound score whose lines are movements of the joints (instruments of "-cs.Robot"):
// "i5 0 0.5 261.626 0 150 0" moves the right arm (instrument 5) from 0 to 150 degrees in 0.5 s. Click a prototype to see its score and properties.
// The grammar places gestures on beats, and the time-setting algorithm adapts each of them according to its properties:


// - "clap" is never rescaled: it keeps its speed at any tempo. Its pivot, the point placed on the beat, is the impact of the hands (150 ms), not its beginning.
// So the hands meet exactly on the beats, the preparation of each clap starting before its beat.
// - "wave" is cyclic and never rescaled: after raising the arm (500 ms), its waving part (500 ms) is repeated as long as the object lasts, rather than slowed down.
// - "nod" can be compressed or expanded, but only between 0.5 and 2 times, as a motor has speed limits.
// - "armsup", "armsdown" and "waveoff" are rescaled freely: they follow the tempo.


// The torso swings with notes and _cont(torso), as in "-gr.robot_dance", to show that notes and time-objects can be combined.
// Every section ends in the rest position (all angles 0).

ORD
gram#1[1] S --> Hello Claps Waves FastClaps Bye


